## Pitfalls

- **12m+7m without TP still misses flux.** "even with the ACA only 50% of the extended flux is recovered"
  (2014A&A...570L..14R); ALMA-ACA recovered 8.4 of ~29 Msun (2018ApJ...856..147O); ACA alone recovered 41% and
  21% of SCUBA-2 flux in two cores (2020ApJ...895..119T); [CI] flux 34±15% lower than Herschel
  (2018ApJ...863..143C); about 4 of 8.2 Jy in APEX CO 3-2 resolved out (2017ApJ...841..110S). Treat masses
  from such maps as lower limits, as 2017ApJ...837...60B did.
- **Missing flux is channel dependent.** Negligible at line edges but 30-40% in central channels
  (2015ApJ...814..143A); the interferometer alone held ~0.15 of the NRO45 flux, the feathered map ~0.8
  (2019ApJ...872..121U). Line ratios between a combined and an uncombined line are biased.
- **Single-dish flux scale is a free parameter in practice.** 2020A&A...635A..71W rescaled a TP map by 0.979
  and still calls the absolute TP scale "less certain"; 2018ApJ...853..171G had to scale SCUBA by ~3.
  Feathering inherits any single-dish calibration error directly into the large-scale flux.
- **Primary beam and mosaic response.** Multiply the single-dish map by the mosaic primary-beam response before
  feathering (2019A&A...623A..96Y). The same paper notes a CASA mosaic imaging issue that overestimated fluxes
  by 10%.
- **Unchecked weights.** Data from different cycles can carry weights that do not reflect sensitivity; papers fixed
  this with `statwt` or manual rescaling to match noise variance (2017A&A...605A..42C; 2019ApJ...887...40W).
- **Positional and frame mismatches** between configurations, epochs or cycles blur structure (see Step 3).
  Moving targets need `fixplanets` (2016ApJ...821L...8S).
- **Pixels in feathered or combined maps are correlated on the beam scale**; 2017ApJ...845L..19B did not
  correct for this in a pixel-by-pixel comparison. Bin to at least a beam before regressions.
- **Settings the cards flag as not stated** (from the pack's excerpts): feathering parameters
  (2020ApJ...890..167T; 2017ApJ...845L..19B), the TP combination method (2020A&A...633A..13D), relative weighting
  of 12-m and ACA (2018ApJ...856..147O; 2019ApJ...875...96N; 2017ApJ...850L...6A; 2021ApJ...908..231M), and
  how APEX data were regridded and scaled for `sdintimaging` (2026ApJ..1003...68Y). The cards rarely state
  `sdfactor`, `effdishdiam` or `sdgain`. Report these yourself.
- **Using combined data where it hurts.** Large-scale emission raises the background for compact-source
  finding; see When not to use.

## Verification checks

What the papers did:

- **Total flux vs single dish.** Combined maps recovered ~90% of APEX flux (2017A&A...605A..28D;
  2020A&A...633A..13D); ALMA total flux consistent with Nobeyama 45-m (2020ApJ...901..151S); missing flux vs IRAM
  30m <~30% north, ~50% south (2020ApJ...903...94M); ~60% of the flux estimated from a 1.2 mm image
  (2017MNRAS.464L..31H).
- **Spectra vs single dish at matched resolution.** Feathered cube profile vs IRAM 30-m at 30"
  (2018ApJ...858...90G); 7M+TP spectrum matched the TP profile (2019PASJ...71...85M); ACA profile vs APEX
  (2016RAA....16..106H); feathering, interferometer-only and NRO45 spectra side by side (2019ApJ...872..121U).
- **Flux-scale agreement on overlapping uv scales**: 10% (2020ApJ...889....9M), 15% (2018ApJ...863..143C).
- **Gain from adding short spacings.** 12m+ACA concatenation recovered 9-24% extra CO over ACA alone in four
  of six sources (2021ApJ...908..231M).
- **Sensitivity to choices.** ACA weight changes did not affect results (2014A&A...570L..14R); SCUBA scale
  factor varied 0.5x-10x (2018ApJ...853..171G); direct Fourier-plane feather tested with no clear improvement
  (2018MNRAS.475..448T); compared with APEX spectra and Hogbom-cleaned individual datasets
  (2019A&A...631A..64B); residual scaling for flux consistency with the TP map (2018ApJ...867..166S).
- **External instruments.** ACA source fluxes agree with MUSTANG-2 within a few percent (2020ApJ...893...13M);
  morphology checked against SMA, SHARC2 and VLA (2015ApJ...804...37L).

What a careful referee adds (general practice, not from the pack):

- Smooth the combined cube to the single-dish beam and compare channel by channel, not only the integrated flux.
- Compare the power spectra or radial uv amplitudes of TP, 7m and 12m in their overlap annulus.
- State which arrays went into every product and the MRS of each, and give flux-recovery fractions per line.
- Check the clean-residual flux scaling (dirty-beam vs clean-beam area) when the combined beam is non-Gaussian.

