### Assumptions (bibcode: value)
- 2018ApJ...853..171G: foreground column 5e21-5e22 cm-2
- 2019Natur.569..519K: alpha_CO = 4.35 (Z/Zsun)^-1 Msun/(K km/s pc^2), 50% uncertainty
- 2020ApJ...895..119T: beta = 1.8 for flux scaling
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Gaussian intensity distribution; uncertainties assume reduced chi2 of 1
- 2017ApJ...850L...6A: Star unresolved; non-thermal emission negligible
- 2017ApJ...850L...6A: Circular belt tilted; T_d ~10 K with same temperature law
- 2019AJ....157..251T: 5% absolute flux error from calibrators
- 2021AJ....161..271F: Dust: 70% astrosilicate, 15% amorphous carbon, 15% water ice; size power law -3.5, 1 um to 1 cm; Band 7 opacity 1.9 cm2/g
- 2021AJ....161..271F: Band 6 emission scaled from Band 7 via free alpha_mm
- 2021AJ....161..271F: Toy model inclination 33 deg, stellar mass 1.56 Msun
- 2019A&A...628A.100D: gamma=5/3; flat LCDM Om=0.30, H0=70; kSZ neglected
- 2015A&A...576L...2S: Missing short-spacing flux negligible
- 2018ApJ...856..147O: Mean molecular weight 2.33
- 2025A&A...700A.165B: Galaxy unresolved at ACA resolution; GMCs co-spatial with star clusters and unresolved
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Optically thin; r^-0.5 temperature profile; constant dust opacity
- 2024ApJ...966..117X: distance 2 kpc
- 2024A&A...692A.215C: Chabrier IMF; flat LCDM Om=0.3, OL=0.7


### Limitations the authors admit
- 2018ApJ...853..171G: Catalog potentially incomplete; completeness cannot be quantified
- 2018ApJ...853..171G: Column density maps not very accurate; SFR strongly dependent on assumed timescale
- 2019Natur.569..519K: Extinction correction might underestimate attenuation toward GMC density peaks
- 2019Natur.569..519K: eps_sf and eta_fb depend on CO-to-H2 and Halpha-to-SFR conversion factors
- 2026ApJ..1003...68Y: H I column densities likely underestimated due to low resolution dilution
- 2019ApJ...875...96N: Observation time was ~20% of the requested time, insufficient to test the model
- 2020ApJ...895..119T: ACA missing flux; limited resolution cannot resolve protoplanetary disk; velocity difference near spectral resolution
- 2020ApJ...889....9M: Resolution cannot exclude that regions comprise unresolved clouds
- 2020ApJ...889....9M: Detailed kinematic characterization left for future work
- 2025ApJ...988..162D: Small sample; individual outliers can affect galaxy-to-galaxy trends
- 2025ApJ...988..162D: Metallicity covers only ~0.25 dex and 8 galaxies
- 2019ApJ...876..130H: Single dust temperature assumed across sources, affecting Sigma_SFR maps
- 2019ApJ...876..130H: Interpretations require kinematic confirmation; small sample
- 2024A&A...690A..55S: Halo mass estimates carry large uncertainties; group centre and concentration degeneracies; interloper contamination
- 2024A&A...690A..55S: Cold-stream regime scatter based on only six points
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Spherical symmetry assumed despite asymmetric emission
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Weak lines too low S/N for uv fitting
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: Distance mismatch between GRS 1915+105 and IRAS source; jet power assumes constant power and density
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: ALMA continuum lacks single-dish data so flux is underestimated
- 2024AJ....167...66Y: Emission only marginally resolved; midplane assumption; CH2DOH spectroscopy uncertain by ~factor 3
- 2020ApJ...889L..24P: Central emission shape may be affected by the PSF; brightest gap feature likely an artefact
- 2017ApJ...850L...6A: Data insufficient for proper modeling; secondary source could be a noise peak
- 2020A&A...635A..71W: Absolute Tb scale from TP remains uncertain
- 2021ApJ...908..231M: Small and possibly biased sample
- 2021ApJ...908..231M: Surface density depends on alpha_CO choice
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Model not formally fit; chosen by eye
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Mass-loss rate is a lower limit as optical depth is about unity
- 2018MNRAS.480.4974H: Coarse ACA resolution cannot resolve pairs closer than 2-3"; physical association unproven
- 2019AJ....157..251T: Models are highly degenerate and omit latitudinal temperature variations and adiabatic heating/cooling
- 2015ApJ...804...37L: Kinematic analysis preliminary since arm inclinations unknown
- 2020ApJ...905...85S: Limited ALMA bandwidth prevents detection of redshifted P Cygni emission and caps vmax
- 2020ApJ...905...85S: Conservative classification is S/N dependent and may exclude weak outflows
- 2015ApJ...808..102K: Inner radii unreliable due to resolution and decoherence; constant beta assumed; kappa0 uncertain by factor two
- 2019ApJ...871..112X: AcA morphology cannot be accurately determined due to few transitions and spatial contamination
- 2019ApJ...871..112X: Spectral simulation parameters chosen subjectively
- 2018MNRAS.481.4931E: Velocity resolution is modest and dynamical modelling is deferred.
- 2021AJ....161..271F: Model-dependent total flux; ALMA flux about half of SCUBA-2 flux
- 2019A&A...628A.100D: Systematics from cluster geometry and complex post-shock gas distribution; model does not capture X-ray morphology
- 2014A&A...570L..14R: Only ~50% of extended flux recovered even with ACA; dynamic range limited to ~50
- 2020ApJ...890..167T: A single source of ~1e4 Msun cannot explain T2 and T3 kinematics; diffuse mass distribution possible
- 2015A&A...576L...2S: Delivered data did not meet requested sensitivity; ~25% flux calibration uncertainty
- 2014ApJ...797...90S: Mass estimates depend on uncertain X_CO; may be an order of magnitude lower if optically thin
- 2017ApJ...845L..19B: Pixels are correlated on ALMA beam scale and not corrected for
- 2017ApJ...845L..19B: Datasets not strictly simultaneous
- 2026A&A...707A.120H: Did not recover high temperatures (>100 K) at the cloud edge; limited angular resolution and sensitivity
- 2026A&A...707A.120H: Uncertainties exclude systematics from fixed parameters
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: HDO and H2O observed ~2 weeks apart; Q(H2O) inferred via CH3OH proxy
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: Low S/N of HDO leaves L_p unconstrained for 50% distributed case
- 2025A&A...696A.100G: Exact chemical pathways and relative contributions of bottom-up and top-down processes remain unquantified; models omit PAH chemistry
- 2025A&A...700A.285W: Torque method unvalidated by simulations, configuration likely unstable
- 2025A&A...700A.285W: Mass of young component is poorly constrained from single UV band; closed-box and alpha_CO assumptions
- 2019MNRAS.488.1005P: System ages uncertain by ~50%
- 2019MNRAS.488.1005P: Gas (CO) not analysed
- 2014ApJ...795L..25R: Core unresolved so density is a lower limit; deviation may be from temperature
- 2017A&A...604A.115V: Flux measurements of 1b+3b are highly uncertain because of source shape
- 2014MNRAS.444.1821F: Early, shallow ALMA data with limited antennas; projections assume no further collisional evolution
- 2018ApJ...856..147O: Missing flux: ALMA-ACA recovers only 8.4 of ~29 Msun, so density profile of ALMA-ACA cannot be discussed.
- 2018ApJ...856..147O: Several condensations not well resolved; radius close to beam size.
- 2018ApJ...863..143C: Some extended [CI] emission resolved out; flux 34±15% lower than Herschel
- 2018ApJ...863..143C: Outflow environment unprecedented; [CI]-based assumptions (X_CI, same gas as CO) uncertain
- 2024ApJ...962...48J: Single-temperature, single-velocity assumption and non-LTE excitation of some lines (5-4) not explored
- 2024ApJ...962...48J: Dust temperature not well known and assumed equal to Trot
- 2018ApJ...869L..41A: Sample is biased to bright, large disks and earlier spectral types, not representative of the general population
- 2018ApJ...869L..41A: CO data not sensitive enough for useful channel maps at best resolution; cloud contamination in many targets
- 2021ApJ...907L..15S: Gas temperature on small scales unknown; velocity resolution insufficient to measure line data at substructure scales.
- 2020ApJ...901..151S: Electron density of ionized gas is uncertain, and xi is difficult to estimate
- 2025A&A...700A.165B: Current data cannot distinguish between scenarios
- 2019ApJ...887...40W: Face-on geometry makes inclination and Vc poorly constrained; M_dyn is a lower limit
- 2025ApJS..278...45F: 1-2 sources may be spurious; no completeness correction for IRLF; z>9 detections marginal
- 2017A&A...605A..28D: Weak bimodal high-velocity emission not reproduced; 12CO 9-8 peak ~20% low; LVG may not apply to torus
- 2019ApJ...872..121U: Abundance uncertainty up to a factor of 2 affects masses
- 2025ApJ...986L..11S: Low S/N; EDDY ignores beam convolution; visibility mass inconsistent with Teff
- 2025ApJ...986L..11S: Substructure tentative; BIC prefers no ring
- 2020ApJ...895..109F: Systematic effects (midplane temperature, flux calibration) dominate over statistical uncertainties.
- 2020ApJ...895..109F: Unresolved central positive residuals and simple density/temperature prescriptions.
- 2019AJ....158..162F: Apocenter-glow detection remains qualitative; lacks sensitivity
- 2019AJ....158..162F: Perturber constraints are degenerate without extra constraint; S1 comoving unknown
- 2021A&A...652A..92N: Observed p-mode rms is a lower limit since resolution is coarse and pixels are correlated
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Common T_dust adopted for all sources; mass estimates depend on assumed conversion factors
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Spectral index maps only possible for 3 sources
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Small-number statistics for orientation and correlations
- 2020A&A...644A..59K: Errors underestimated; isothermal assumption fails in center; SO2 fits unsatisfactory
- 2020A&A...644A..59K: Beam filling factors set to 1; no collisions with e- and H
- 2016A&A...586A..70L: Irregular, sparse time sampling prevents robust variability analysis; VI are lower limits.
- 2016ApJ...821L...8S: Unquantified systematic errors (disc-averaged temperature, Voigt profile, line-broadening coefficients)
- 2015Natur.527...70P: Inclination unknown and constant-velocity assumption
- 2020A&A...641A.155V: LVG parameters highly degenerate; best-fit values reflect relative trends only
- 2020A&A...641A.155V: Sample biased to upper main sequence and warm dust by PACS detection requirement
- 2015ApJ...812..126C: Absolute flux scale uncertain, affecting spectral index and optical depths
- 2017A&A...597A..53L: Tex hard to constrain for propanal and acetone; uncertainties dominated by LTE and Gaussian assumptions
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Peak brightness cannot be converted to density without non-LTE excitation modelling, which needs more than one line.
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Models are non-rotating and omit chemistry, so SASI signatures cannot be assessed.
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Total belt flux is model-dependent due to extrapolation to zero uv distance; position angle and inclination unconstrained
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Low target elevation and antenna shadowing
- 2016PASJ...68...88K: Missing flux on large scales due to no Total Power Array
- 2015ApJ...814..143A: Smooth spherical shell model does not reproduce fine structure; infrared pumping only partly included
- 2020ApJS..251...14H: Completeness assumes point sources and does not capture extended emission; masses uncertain by factor ~2
- 2015ApJ...811..124S: Systematic uncertainties in alpha_CO ~100% per method
- 2015ApJ...803...60S: alpha_CO very uncertain and held constant
- 2015ApJ...803...60S: Missing flux for some lines
- 2017ApJ...850...35L: Side lobes may affect 1.3 mm umbral brightness, which should be treated as an upper limit
- 2019ApJ...874...89C: Mass uncertainty ~50% due to distance and opacity
- 2019ApJ...874...89C: Smooth model underestimates peak flux because extended structure is filtered
- 2018ApJ...858...90G: Sample not representative; simple alpha_CO and alpha_HCN; limited to inner few kpc
- 2024ApJ...966..117X: Single 60 Msun core evolutionary sequence; PDR effects ignored; fitted masses not reliable
- 2018ApJ...852..122H: Models are not optimal; dust modeling and multi-line fitting deferred; perturbed temperature model not physically self-consistent
- 2018ApJ...852..122H: Absolute alpha uncertain by ~0.4 from flux calibration
- 2021A&A...648A..41V: Outflow masses are lower limits (no correction for missing flux at cloud velocities or opacity); sample not statistically significant.
- 2025MNRAS.541.2540Z: Circular-orbit assumption with mild non-circular motions; distance uncertainty (10%) not included in budget
- 2019PASJ...71...71H: M_dyn uncertain by at least a factor of three; virial theorem may not apply.
- 2019PASJ...71...71H: Clump continuum fluxes may be contaminated by each other at current resolution.
- 2024ApJ...972..147C: LVG parameters highly degenerate; large uncertainty in non-thermal index; unknown CI excitation
- 2017ApJ...841..110S: Envelope size only a lower limit because CO is in absorption
- 2019ApJ...885L..20H: Regions filled with nuclear filaments are small, so shear and non-rotating clumps could be present
- 2024ApJ...976..132H: FUV fields are upper bounds from projected separations; temperature uncertainty dominates dust-trap and planet-mass estimates; SVI is approximate
- 2021ApJ...908....8C: Gas mass is valid within the model framework; CO fractionation not included; inclination not explored
- 2019ApJ...881...84S: Outlier conclusion sensitive to Gaussian intrinsic scatter assumption; large age uncertainty affects masses
- 2020ApJ...888L..28S: Width comparable to beam, so the actual width may be narrower
- 2020ApJ...888L..28S: Only relative brightness temperatures because single-dish data not combined
- 2020ApJ...892L..18I: Core component interpretation not conclusive.

